Every clinician should discuss a periodic-opioid-reassessment with a patient.
Every clinician should assess an opioid-goal-attainment during a periodic-opioid-reassessment.
If a patient has an ineffective-opioid-therapy then every clinician should consider an opioid-taper and should consider a dosage-reduction and should consider a discontinuation and should consider an additional-nonpharmacologic-treatment and should consider an additional-nonopioid-pharmacologic-treatment.
If a patient has a harmful-opioid-therapy then every clinician should consider an opioid-taper and should consider a dosage-reduction and should consider a discontinuation and should consider an additional-nonpharmacologic-treatment and should consider an additional-nonopioid-pharmacologic-treatment.
